From 943eee699732c6eed7be688b7f318a4ff030669d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:11:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(tools): draw a milling tool's cutter, neck and shank as
 a spun profile

#93 slice 2 (slice 1, the drawn holder, was #475). A milling tool's own
shape is now a drawn spun half-outline beside its numbers:

- camcraft-tools cutter_profile: the agreement law - refused by name when
  the outline is no spun profile, is on a turning tool, leaves the tip,
  is not exactly the stated diameter within the flutes, does not end at
  flute + shank length, is wider than the stated shank above the flutes,
  or folds over itself; parametric() is the numbers' own outline.
- schema::ToolCutter + app::tool_cutter (display only: no generator or
  law reads it; a drawn cutter moves no operation stamp).
- SetToolCutter, one undo step; ChangeTool refuses a number edit that
  would break a drawn cutter; DeleteTool / DeleteEntity restore it.
- MCP get_tool_cutter_profile / set_tool_cutter_profile.
- Project: additive `cutter` key on the tool record, no version step.
- Tool editor Profile tab: Draw holder / Draw cutter, Parametric /
  Custom, the shared flat side view, live refusal, Apply cutter.

Refs #93

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
